# The local stack only (P1.34c): the app host, served with the dev leaf like the PDS host, so the PDS can fetch the
# app's client metadata over HTTPS and verify it against the one dev root it trusts (architecture record
# 2026-10-12-refocus-local-signin-rulings, ruling 1 and Amendment 1). Mounted read-only into sites/enabled by the local
# stack only (P1.34d; C18 under --env local, P1.27l); never copied into the image. Its name and upstream come from the
# environment, with no default. Like the PDS site it applies the zones first and drops the client's address before
# web (snippets/upstream.caddy), so web reads only the edge's socket address. The app sets its own CSP (P1.08).
{$APP_HOST} {
	import tls
	import access-log
	import security-headers
	route {
		import pds-ratelimit
		import upstream {$APP_UPSTREAM}
	}
}
